1
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,049
Sweets here.

2
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:34,781
What are you looking at?

3
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,153
Looking at the path.

4
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:38,387
The path is up ahead.

5
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,320
Am I not looking ahead right now?

6
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:51,187
Aunty, I'll take one of these, please.

7
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:51,883
Sure.

8
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,547
I saw you wanted to eat this last time.

9
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:19,790
Is it good?

10
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,169
It's better than I thought.

11
00:01:24,310 --> 00:01:25,304
Do you want to eat it, Kaew?

12
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,196
Give it a try.

13
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:05,421
Is that what you want?

14
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:10,436
No, I just think it looks cute.

15
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,544
What?

16
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,913
My salary just came in,

17
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,529
so I want to give you something.

18
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,076
Thank you, Kaew.

19
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,941
I will keep it safe.

20
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:44,664
But before we head back,

21
00:02:46,252 --> 00:02:48,006
I want to take you somewhere.

22
00:02:58,289 --> 00:02:58,916
Here is your water.

23
00:02:59,704 --> 00:03:01,107
Thank you, Ming.

24
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:10,443
Kaew!!!

25
00:03:14,313 --> 00:03:15,341
Who did you bring with you?

26
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:21,138
This is Rinkham, Lord Wisanu's daughter.

27
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:24,775
Hello, my lady.

28
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:29,920
Dad, Dad, be careful.

29
00:03:29,963 --> 00:03:30,886
What is it?

30
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:31,920
You don't need to get up.

31
00:03:31,956 --> 00:03:35,600
Oh, I'm feeling much stronger now.

32
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:51,827
This is Lady Rinkham, my master.

33
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,347
It's delicious.

34
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:39,378
It’s just ordinary food.

35
00:04:39,940 --> 00:04:42,196
You probably aren't used to it, my lady.

36
00:04:43,290 --> 00:04:45,815
No, not at all. We have it at my house too.

37
00:04:46,270 --> 00:04:48,609
I have Kaew make it for me regularly.

38
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:50,793
I like it so much—

39
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:53,058
even more than the food at my own home.

40
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,720
And does Kaew do a good job?

41
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,452
Very good, sir.

42
00:05:06,196 --> 00:05:08,190
The best I’ve ever seen.

43
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:15,076
She takes excellent care of me, both as a caretaker

44
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:21,803
and… a close confidant.

45
00:05:34,633 --> 00:05:37,753
If Kaew takes such good care of you, young lady,

46
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,147
then my mind is at ease.

47
00:05:46,030 --> 00:05:50,609
I never would have thought Kaew could do this job so well.

48
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:55,230
Aside from her father, she's never given anyone special care before.

49
00:05:57,187 --> 00:05:57,846
Ming!

50
00:05:58,756 --> 00:05:59,280
What?

51
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,206
I'm praising you here

52
00:06:03,593 --> 00:06:07,643
At first, I didn't think you'd be able to look after me either.

53
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:14,055
But when the time came, you turned out to be the most reliable person.

54
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:02,049
Kaew,

55
00:07:05,163 --> 00:07:08,203
she isn't just your master, is she?

56
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:10,990
What do you mean?

57
00:07:15,490 --> 00:07:17,366
I’ve seen right through you from the very beginning.

58
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:21,507
You don't look at her the way you look at anyone else.

59
00:07:26,410 --> 00:07:29,470
I shouldn't be feeling this way, should I?

60
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,526
What shouldn't you feel?

61
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,292
Is it because of status,

62
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:37,489
or because she's a woman?

63
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,400
Both.

64
00:07:45,513 --> 00:07:47,510
I shouldn't feel this way at all, Ming.

65
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:53,341
Can we really choose our feelings?

66
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,738
Let me tell you something.

67
00:07:57,550 --> 00:08:02,049
Loving someone is never right or wrong.

68
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:07,107
There are only people brave enough to accept it.

69
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:14,000
Don't think for a second that I would look down on you.

70
00:08:15,030 --> 00:08:24,258
In fact, I'm glad you have someone who looks at you that way.

71
00:08:35,630 --> 00:08:38,750
My daughter is brave,

72
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,609
but she lacked opportunity.

73
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:45,058
Ever since her mother passed away,

74
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,895
Kaew had to do everything himself.

75
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:50,904
I couldn't help her much either.

76
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:56,855
I must thank you, Lady, for giving her a chance.

77
00:08:58,061 --> 00:09:00,060
I didn't give her the opportunity.

78
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:04,326
She was the one who seized it herself.

79
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:09,704
If you put it that way, I can rest easy.

80
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:14,941
Please take care of her, Lady.

81
00:09:17,110 --> 00:09:18,793
I will take care of her myself,

82
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:21,723
no matter in what capacity.

83
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:33,827
Your family is so warm;

84
00:09:34,270 --> 00:09:35,618
I've never seen anything like this before.

85
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:41,507
I must thank you too, for showing me a whole new world.

86
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:49,107
In that case, let's race!

87
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:51,649
Race what?

88
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,104
Whoever gets back to the house first wins.

89
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:56,516
And if you lose...

90
00:09:57,300 --> 00:10:00,886
tonight, you will be punished.

91
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:02,861
Rinkham!

92
00:10:12,172 --> 00:10:13,101
Rinkham,

93
00:10:15,110 --> 00:10:16,123
come here for a moment, dear.

94
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:26,012
This is Khun Chai Phakdee.

95
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:29,975
From now on, he will be your fiancé.	
